      'Name the actual danger points, since plain JSX text interpolation is safe by default: dangerouslySetInnerHTML with any user- or third-party-influenced content, href/src attributes built from user input (a javascript: URL), and any place raw HTML is injected outside React entirely (a CMS-rendered field, an innerHTML call in a ref effect, a third-party widget\'s injected markup).',
